   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are clean \u2014 DRC 0, LVS match at every point.\n\n## Final status\n\nThe `nand2` standard cell is complete at `/nand2.icl` and passes both DRC and LVS at the nominal point and across the full sweep (L=0.18/0.25, widths \u00d70.85/\u00d71.35/\u00d71.9, H up to 4.08).\n\n**What was hard:** Getting the stick plan right for the fixed netlist. The key insight was that both rows share the same gate order (A, B) with one poly gate crossing both diffusions per lesson 10, and that Y appears at the n-row left end but the p-row middle \u2014 so it doesn't line up and must be joined with `route Y layers=m1,m2` rather than a strap (lesson 6). The gate-contact bottom `cb` had to be computed from n-row items only (lesson 1) to avoid pushing contacts into the n-tap row. The diffusion span derives from L and the gaps so it follows the sweep, and `width=4` columns (0.46 \u00b5m each) was sufficient to fit everything at L=0.25.",
