   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points pass DRC and LVS cleanly. The inverter layout is complete.\n\n**Final status:** `/inv.icl` is clean at the nominal point and across the entire sweep (L=0.18/0.25, widths x0.85/1.35/1.9, H=2.72/3.26/4.08).\n\n**What was hard:** The main challenge was avoiding the gate-contact/output-strap proximity conflict (li.3, mcon.2) and the SHORT between nets. Key fixes:\n- Placed sources (VGND/VPWR) on the left of the gate and drains (Y) on the right, so the output strap runs vertically on the right side of the gate.\n- Shifted the gate contact left by 0.13 \u00b5m (`cx=(g1.cx - 0.13)`) away from the right-side output strap, per lesson 11.\n- Restricted `cb` to n-row items only (`max(nd1.top + 0.19, c1l.top + 0.25)`), per lesson 1 \u2014 including the p-row contact pushed the gate contact up into the n-tap row.\n- Placed the Y port mcon on the output strap at the p-row center height (`cy=(py1 - WP/2)`) to avoid mcon.2 conflicts with the gate-contact mcon at gate-contact height, per lesson 13.\n- Used `width=5` columns (2.3 \u00b5m) which fits at L=0.25 as required.",
