   "final_message": "Final status: **CLEAN** \u2014 `/nand3.icl` passes DRC (0 violations) and LVS (match) at all 6 sweep points.\n\n**What was hard:** The main challenge was resolving the DRC conflict between the output Y strap (at column 0, where Y lines up in both n and p rows) and the gate-A contact li. Per lesson 11, I shifted all gate contacts right by 0.13 \u00b5m to clear the strap, which then caused poly.2 violations between neighboring gate-contact pads. I fixed this by adding 0.13 \u00b5m to the inter-gate pitch (`max(0.28, 0.54 - L + 0.13)`). The internal nets n1/n2 were handled by labeling their drain strips and gate contacts with the same net name and routing them (`route n1/n2 layers=m1,m2`), and Y's second p-row occurrence was connected via `route Y`. The layout stays clean across the full parameter sweep (L=0.15\u20130.25, widths \u00d70.85\u20131.9, H=2.72\u20134.08).",
