   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are clean (DRC 0, LVS match at every point).\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilt `/nor3.icl` \u2014 a standard-cell layout of `nor3` (Y = !(A|B|C)) following the fixed SkyWater netlist.\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- **Gate order A,B,C** in both rows (n-row: `VGND [A] Y [B] VGND [C] Y`; p-row: `VPWR [A] n1 [B] n2 [C] Y`), so output Y lines up at right-of-C in both rows and can be joined by a single vertical `strap li`.\n- **Intermediate diffusion columns** between gates labelled with their nets (n1, n2) so LVS matches \u2014 the n-row's Y/VGND columns and p-row's n1/n2 columns each get li strips with matching `net=` labels.\n- **Output strap shifted clear of gate C's contact** by shifting all gate contacts left by 0.13 \u00b5m together (keeping their mutual spacing), avoiding li.3/li.c2 shorts.\n- **Gate pitch parameterized** as `pitch = max(0.60, 0.545 + L/2)` so the 0.33 \u00b5m gate-contact pads stay \u2265 0.21 \u00b5m from neighbouring poly gates across the whole sweep (critical at L=0.25).\n- **width=6 columns** (2.76 \u00b5m) fits the diffusion span at L=0.25.\n- Ports A/B/C on met1 pads over gate contacts; port Y on the routed met1 of the strap; `route Y layers=m1,m2` and `route n2 layers=m1,m2` for the internal series node.\n\nThe hardest part was balancing the gate-contact shift (to clear the output strap) against poly-to-poly spacing between pads and neighbouring gates \u2014 solved by scaling the gate pitch with L.",
