   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are clean \u2014 DRC 0, LVS match at every point.\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilt `/a21oi.icl` for the `a21oi` cell (Y = !((A1 & A2) | B1)) following the verified `o21ai` pattern:\n\n**Structure:**\n- Gate order A2, A1, B1 shared by both rows (one poly gate per net crossing both nd/pd rows, one gate contact each).\n- **n row:** single diffusion island VGND|A2|n1|A1|Y|B1|VGND (all series nodes share a node).\n- **p row:** split into two islands VPWR|A2|n2|A1|VPWR | VPWR|n2|B1|Y because n2 and VPWR can't share a column across the break (0.80 \u00b5m gap between g2 and g3).\n- Internal nets n1 and n2 are routed (`route n1/n2 layers=m1,m2`) since their drain strips don't line up with their gate contacts; Y is routed too since n-row Y and p-row Y don't align.\n- Supply columns (VGND, VPWR) each get contact arrays and straps to the rails.\n- Gate contacts placed at `cb = max(nd.top + 0.19, <li>.top + 0.25)` using only n-row items; all gate contacts enclosed in one `npc`.\n- Input ports on met1 over gate contacts; output pin on the routed met1.\n\n**Hard part:** Getting the p-row island break right \u2014 n2 must be routed (not strapped) across the break, and the gate order had to work for both rows simultaneously. The sweep (including L=0.25 with width=7 columns and the wider H=4.08 point) passed cleanly on the first try.",
