   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are clean. The layout is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilt `/a22oi.icl` for the `a22oi` cell (Y = !((A1&A2)|(B1&B2))) using the verified example patterns as a template.\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- **Gate order A2\u2013B2\u2013B1\u2013A1** on both rows, matching the series-node structure of both networks.\n- **One diffusion break** between g1 (A2) and g2 (B2) on the n-row (0.80 \u00b5m gap), because n3 (right of A2) and VGND (left of B2) cannot share an island. The p-row stays a single island since all its adjacent series nodes match (n2 between A2/B2 and B1/A1).\n- **Correct net labels** on every drain/source contact column derived from the fixed transistor netlist (this fixed the initial LVS mismatches).\n- **width=8 columns** (3.68 \u00b5m) chosen so the p-diffusion keeps \u22650.18 \u00b5m from the n-well edge even at L=0.25 (width=7 failed diff/tap.8 there).\n- All four internal nets (n1, n2, n3, Y) routed with `route ... layers=m1,m2 prefer=m2`; output pin Y placed on the routed met1.\n\n**Result:** DRC 0 + LVS match at nominal, and all 6 sweep points clean (L=0.18/0.25, widths \u00d70.85/\u00d71.35/\u00d71.9 with H=2.72/3.26/4.08).",
